  <li class="done"><b>500M post-pretrain refine pipeline — ALL THREE NULL (2026-07-11).</b> PMA soup: val_ppl 15.5534&rarr;15.5472 (-0.006, negligible). MQAR-refine: recall_eval flat at every N, memory-Δ never approached its +40 target. Sparsity-refine: spike 0.069&rarr;0.069, never approached 0.05 target. Verified not a measurement artifact (arch-kwargs bug in <code>recall_eval.py</code> fixed, train/eval token-range consistency + sample-size sufficiency checked). Likely budget, not uselessness — literature mid-training phases run 27B+ tokens. Test 2 (<code>mqar_refine_500m_strong.yaml</code>, 4&times; budget) currently running to settle budget-vs-architectural-ceiling. See <code>neuro_500m_post_pretrain_refine_null.md</code>.</li>
  <li class="done"><b>90M MoR seed1 beta-fix validation (2026-07-10).</b> Decisively confirmed at 4-layer scale. 9 consecutive evals, all 4 blocks dead_frac 0% every time; memory-Δ peaked +206.38 (settled ~+175); val_ppl 104.98→52.77. See journey.html &sect;35.</li>
  <li class="done"><b>β-collapse recipe fix SHIPPED as <code>beta_floor: 0.1</code></b> (2026-07-10, seed-confirmed at 30M + 90M). Root cause: scalar β = sigmoid(W_β·spk) saturates below -20 → β bit-zero → M never written → memory contributes exactly 0. NVIDIA's Gated DeltaNet-2 (arXiv:2605.22791) diagnosis, discovered independently a week earlier. Was affecting <b>every 30M+ delta-rule screen we'd run</b>. Fix1 (<code>beta_floor=0.1</code>) 30M win: val_ppl 65.87 vs baseline 76.43 (<b>-10.6 ppl</b>), memory-Δ +94.44 vs +2.35 (~40× recovery), β dead_frac = <b>0%</b> across the whole run. Fix2 (vector_beta) SKIPPED — sequential loop OOMs at any reasonable batch on 16GB, and fix1 was decisive. Landed: β telemetry in <code>train_gpu.evaluate()</code> prints <code>[beta] blk0: μ=... dead=X%</code> after each <code>[eval]</code> and marks <code>COLLAPSED</code> if dead_frac≥95%; <code>beta_floor: 0.1</code> baked into all queued A/B configs; 90M seed1 validation on the exact fully-collapsed failure mode confirmed the fix holds. <b>Standing rule:</b> every new spiking <code>delta_rule</code> config should include <code>beta_floor: 0.1</code>; default 0.0 recovers the collapse pathology. Full writeup: <code>journey.html</code> §33.</li>
  <li class="done"><b>WSL memory-cap gotcha (2026-07-11).</b> <code>.wslconfig</code> capped memory at 20GB despite 32GB host RAM, causing silent OOM-kills mid-session (misread initially as environment instability). Bumped to 24GB. See <code>reference_wsl_memory_config.md</code>.</li>
  <li class="done"><b>350M-MoR-checkpoint recall_eval and KD-on-350M — folded into the restart-vs-replan decision (2026-07-11).</b> Both were open items on the assumption the current paused 350M would resume; both are now conditional on the (a)/(b) choice above and no longer stand alone as separate to-dos. If (a) resume, the paused ckpt gets <code>recall_eval.py</code>; if (b) replan, the KD-add decision is redone against the new plan.</li>
  <li class="done"><b>Recurrent-depth Phase 0/1 closed negative, seed-confirmed.</b> Fair depth-1@200M (74.55/73.35) beats uniform depth-2 and depth-2+deep-sup — uniform looping closed negative. Literature re-check confirms the closure applies only to uniform looping, not MoR's actual per-token adaptive-routing claim.</li>
